medieval-burned-crown-desc = The metal is scorched and melted in places.

medieval-knight-crown-name = strange circlet, warm to the touch and shimmering with a barely visible light
medieval-knight-crown-desc = a warrior's circlet shaped like a crown

medieval-field-journal-name = field journal
medieval-field-journal-desc = A battered notebook bound in thick pigskin, soaked through with damp and dried blood. Its pages are smeared with grime, soot, and greasy fingerprints. The handwriting is heavy and cramped, but near the end it breaks into uneven, trembling strokes.
medieval-field-journal-content = [bold]Day One.[/bold]

    {"We dug in by the passage to the cellar. Sergeant Brom ordered us to choke the way with sandbags and brace the wooden grate with crates. Rot and dung blow up from the caves - sure sign the greenskin whoresons are close. Six of us. Crossbows oiled, enough bolts to stud the whole road. Let us see how those naked wretches dance against legionary steel."}

    {"[bold]Day Three.[/bold]"}

    {"They come on, sons of bitches, like mad wasps after ale. Yesterday we beat back three waves. We fought in the passage itself, shoulder to shoulder. Goblin filth climbs over its own dead to reach us. Derwin took a sharpened rusty bar under the ribs - the armor held, but now he breathes in a rasp and spits blood."}

    {"We improvised: poured a keg of mountain oil before the barricade and threw a torch. Gods, the shrieking! Those wretches burn well enough, crackling as they go. The stink, though, could drive saints from their shrines."}

    {"[bold]Day Five.[/bold]"}

    {"[color=#8b0000]▓▒░██▒░[/color] things are going badly. The grate is smashed to splinters. Only the bags still hold. Green beasts keep coming without end. Last night they dragged old Runge into the dark before we could make a sound. We heard only bones cracking."}

    {"The bolts are gone. Now it is war picks and thrown mining tools. If those rear-line arseholes upstairs do not send reinforcements, this is where we die. No food left. The hardtack has bloomed white with mold. We swallow spit and break goblin skulls."}

    {"[bold]Day Six.[/bold]"}

    {"Three of us remain. Me, Brom, and young Kevan. The sergeant has no left eye, only a dirty rag around his head, but he will not loose his axe. He growls that we had better not start pissing ourselves."}

    {"The beasts have gone quiet. Gathering together. In the dark I hear hundreds of claws scraping and rusty iron clattering."}

    {"[color=#8b0000]██▓▒░░▒▓██[/color]"}

    {"[bold]Day... something.[/bold]"}

    {"Sergeant Brom gave up his soul to the gods an hour ago. Bled out in my lap. Before he died, he told me to tell his woman he hid his savings under the anvil in the barracks."}

    {"Kevan has curled up behind a crate. He is near gone. Both my hands are cut so badly my fingers can barely hold the quill."}

    {"I hear them. Coming. The rumble reaches from the very[color=#8b0000]▓▒░████[/color]"}

    {"[color=#8b0000]░▒▓██████████████████████████████▓▒░[/color]"}

medieval-scwatter-diary-name = squatter's diary
medieval-scwatter-diary-desc = A coverless notebook swollen with damp. The paper is furred with grey mold and smells of stagnant water, rot, and burnt cloth. The handwriting is twitchy and crooked; many words are misspelled or struck out with rough strokes. Dried stains and crushed insect marks speckle the pages.
medieval-scwatter-diary-content = [bold]Another day in the dark.[/bold]

    {"Set my tent at the very end of the tunnel, past the bend. Quieter here. Less wind. It dripped from above again. The tunnel flooded up to my ankles, and every rag in the tent is wet. Burning old boards for a fire. Smoke eats the eyes, but at least it is warm. Hid the crate of goods so the bandits in the next cave would stop staring. They threatened to come by night and take my place, but they have not dared yet. I only hear them eating and yelling through the wall. Psia krew."}

    {"Yesterday I caught two fat sewer rats. The meat is tough and stinks of slime and rot, but if you char it well enough, it can be eaten. Strip the skin first, so the parasites do not choke you. [color=#555555]░▒▓[/color] my belly has twisted for two days, but that is better than dying of hunger in the Upper City while those bearded bastards stuff themselves."}

    {"[color=#555555]▓▒░██▒░[/color]"}

    {"Heard steps in the tunnel. Someone came down from above. Clean sort. Soft boots, not stomping, stepping. Looking for something, or simply lost. Thinks that because this place reeks of shit, no one lives here."}

    {"Fool. There is always someone in the Sewers. We see everything."}

    {"I held my breath behind the tent. I have rope and a saw. If that softling comes closer to my light, I will have a new jacket. And maybe a little fresh, sweet meat, if the deep rats do not gnaw him first."}

    {"[bold]No one takes my burrow.[/bold] Let them try - they stay here forever. [color=#333333]████▓▒░[/color]"}

medieval-miner-diary-name = miner's diary
medieval-miner-diary-desc = A thick notebook in a leather cover roughened by stone dust. The pages are damp, spotted with mold and dried blood. The entries stop near the middle; the last lines are pressed so hard with graphite that the paper is torn through.
medieval-miner-diary-content = [bold]Third day after the cave-in.[/bold]

    {"The collapse trapped us in the farthest gallery. The eastern tunnel came down clean, tons of stone sealing the passage. Picks are broken. Four of us left: me, old Ivo, young Tim, and Kasper. We burn the last fat in the lamps. Lick water from the walls, but our bellies are empty. Ivo is bad. The rock crushed his chest. We sit in the dark and wait for help."}

    {"[bold]Day Seven.[/bold]"}

    {"No help. Up above, they have likely sung us dead and scratched our names from the rolls. Ivo passed yesterday. We are so weak we cannot even drag him aside."}

    {"Kasper has sat over the body since morning. His eyes are wild and sunken. He mutters that the gods would forgive us, because we must survive. I threatened him with a piece of a pickaxe and told him not to think of that mortal sin. We are honest miners, not ghouls."}

    {"[bold]Day... I do not know.[/bold]"}

    {"[color=#8b0000]▓▒░██▒░[/color] I slept too deeply. Woke to a wet crunching in the dark."}

    {"Kasper did it. He was eating old Ivo, growling and smacking like a stray dog. Young Tim tried to pull him away from the corpse, but Kasper... gods, where did such awful strength come from in a starving body? He hurled the lad into the wall. I heard the crack."}

    {"I squeezed into a narrow cleft between the supports. Kasper sits in the middle of the cave. He is changing before my eyes. I hear his bones stretching and breaking with a vile crackle, his leather jacket splitting around him. An inhuman grave-cold stench begins to pour from him."}

    {"[bold]Last entry.[/bold]"}

    {"He ate them both. But the cursed cannibal missed the one thing that matters."}

    {"Even after selling his soul to the Abyss and becoming a three-meter horned horror, he cannot claw through solid stone with bare hands. He is trapped here. Same as me. I hear him throw himself at the fall in blind rage, flaying the flesh from his new paws, howling with endless, unquenched hunger."}

    {"My lamp is dying. Soon he will smell my breath in the corner."}

    {"[color=#8b0000]Eat me, beast. You will still die in this stone trap.[/color]"}

    {"[color=#333333]░▒▓█████████████████████████████▓▒░[/color]"}

medieval-raider-diary-name = raider's diary
medieval-raider-diary-desc = A dented notebook filled with a crooked bandit's hand. Elegant but very angry comments are written in red ink along the margins.
medieval-raider-diary-content = [color=#5c4033]Yesterday we looted the tower of that dead mage. Found no gold, only this strange little white floating book. Thought I might sell it on the black market, but the damned thing will not shut up! It complains about the stink in our camp, criticizes how I hold the quill, and keeps screaming that I must not dare call it the [italic]\"White Book\"[/italic].

    {"[color=#8b0000][bolditalic]For my true name is Grimoire Weiss, you unhewn lump of dung! Show some respect, or I shall pepper you with Dark Bolts until not even your fleas remain![/bolditalic][/color]"}

    {"And this flying wastepaper also demands that we stop swearing. Says our curses cramp his binding and remind him of some [color=#a0522d]mad rude woman in her underclothes[/color] who swung two swords around."}

    {"[color=#8b0000][bolditalic]Do not even remind me of her! And for all that is holy, stop using participial phrases when you do not know how they work![/bolditalic][/color]"}

    {"Need to palm this cursed folio off on some clever fool before my head splits from listening to it.[/color]"}

medieval-old-foliant-name = liber primordialis
medieval-old-foliant-desc = A massive folio bound in scales from an unknown creature. Its yellowed parchment pages breathe a faint heat, and the letters seem burned into the very fabric of reality.
medieval-old-foliant-content = [center][color=#8b5a2b][head=2]Chronicles of the First Flame[/head][/color][/center]

    {"[color=#1a1a1a]In the Age of Ancients, the world was unformed and veiled in fog. It was a land of grey crags, giant trees, and Everlasting Dragons."}

    {"But then came [color=#c0392b][bold]Fire[/bold][/color]. And with Fire came Disparity. Heat and cold, life and death, and of course... Light and Dark."}

    {"Then from the Dark They came, and within the Flame they found the Souls of Lords:"}

    {"[bullet] [color=#8b0000][bold]Valtor[/bold][/color], God of War and Violence, with his fearless warriors."}

    {"[bullet] [color=#006400][bold]Terra[/bold][/color], Goddess of Earth and Fertility."}

    {"[bullet] [color=#4b0082][bold]Morbius[/bold][/color], God of Death and Decay, first of the dead."}

    {"[bullet] And [color=#4a5d23][bold]Nexar[/bold][/color], so easily forgotten."}

    {"With the strength of Lords, they challenged the Dragons. Valtor's unbreakable might shattered their stone scales. Terra brought down the fury of nature itself and the roots of the primal trees. Morbius released the miasma of death and rot. And [color=#5c5c5c][bold]White Mascot[/bold][/color] betrayed his own, and the Dragons were no more."}

    {"Thus began the Age of Fire. But soon the flame will fade, and only Dark will remain. Even now only embers are left, and man sees not light, but endless nights. And among the living are those who bear the accursed mark..."}

    {"[center][color=#2f4f4f]░░▒▓▓▓[/color][/center][/color]"}

