medieval-goblin-throne-name = goblin throne
medieval-goblin-throne-desc = There is hardly a single gram of gold in it.

medieval-travel-diary-name = desperate traveler's notes
medieval-travel-diary-desc = A crumpled sheet of parchment covered in small, nervous handwriting. In places the paper is rubbed through, as if the writer pressed the quill down with all his rage.
medieval-travel-diary-content = [color=#1a1a1a]I cannot take this anymore. These glowing messages on the ground are driving me mad. Who leaves them? Spirits? Demons?

    {"Yesterday in the dungeon I found a message: [color=#b8860b][bolditalic]\"Secret path ahead\"[/bolditalic][/color]. I spent two hours hammering a dead stone wall with my fists and pick until my knuckles bled. There was nothing there!"}

    {"By the river I found a rune that read: [color=#b8860b][bolditalic]\"Beware of dog!\"[/bolditalic][/color]. I drew my sword and readied myself for mortal combat with a hound, and in the bushes sat an ordinary old turtle, slowly chewing grass!"}

    {"And this morning... We stood at the edge of a bottomless chasm. Right by the drop, a message glowed: [color=#b8860b][bolditalic]\"Try jump, treasure ahead\"[/bolditalic][/color]. My companion, idiot that he was, believed it. I can still hear his fading scream."}

    {"But the most insulting one waited when I returned to camp. Someone had scratched this beside my bedroll: [color=#b8860b][bolditalic]\"You have no maiden\"[/bolditalic][/color]."}

    {"By the [color=#d4af37][bold]Golden Tree[/bold][/color], if I find the jester leaving these signs, I will shove his rotten finger straight up his [color=#888888]██▓▒░[/color][/color]"}

medieval-damaged-paper-name = ravaged parchment
medieval-damaged-paper-desc = The parchment's edges are rimed with frost that will not melt, and blood has dried along the bottom. A clerk's neat hand in the middle gives way to rough, panicked charcoal scrawls.
medieval-damaged-paper-content = [head=3][bold]GUILD DIRECTIVE[/bold][/head]

    {"[bold]Sector:[/bold] Deep Workings (Level 4-B)."}

    {"[bold]Status:[/bold] Quarantine. The site is to be sealed."}

    {"[bold]Order:[/bold]"}

    {"Cease all excavation in the cavern containing the \"Stag Horns\" skeleton. Leave all tools and winches in place. Block the gallery with three layers of oak beams and seal it with warding runes of the Order of Purification."}

    {"[bold]Justification:[/bold]"}

    {"Five tunnelers vanished into the dark in a single shift. The three survivors show signs of hunger-curse and uncontrolled aggression. The field physician confirmed the presence of corruption: the infected's teeth have sharpened, their flesh is paling, and body temperature is unnaturally..."}

    {"[color=#555555]═════════════════════════════════════[/color]"}

    {"[color=#3a3a3a][bold]WE WILL NOT LET IT OUT.[/bold][/color]"}

    {"[color=#3a3a3a]We nailed shut the main passage and raised barricades. If you hear claws scraping behind the boards, or the voice of your friend begging to be let in because he is [/color][color=#8b0000][bold]\"so terribly hungry\"[/bold][/color][color=#3a3a3a] - [bold]DO NOT LISTEN.[/bold] Take axes and strike through the gaps until it falls silent. [/color]"}

    {"[color=#3a3a3a]The spirit of that thing seeks new flesh. If the boarded planks begin to frost from within, the runes have fallen. Run for the exit and do not look back.[/color]"}

    {"[color=#8b0000][bold] ░▒▓██ WHOEVER FINDS THIS - LEAVE ██▓▒░ [/bold][/color]"}

medieval-oldie-paper-name = old parchment
medieval-oldie-paper-content = [italic]

    {"ATTENTION, GUARDS!"}

    {"There are goblins in cell number two. THREE OF THEM. Separate them from each other, for the sake of all gods!"}

    {"Yesterday they managed to:"}

    {"1. Unscrew the cell bars using one of their own jaws. (The jaw was later found under the bunks - it had not a single tooth left, but the hole remained)."}

    {"2. Trade clothes with the rats. (The rats are now sitting in the cell wearing goblin trousers, while the goblins crawl around the cellar)."}

    {"3. Teach the recruit on watch that the goblin word for \"freedom\" means \"I am peaceful and unarmed\". The recruit let them out for a walk. We barely caught them."}

    {"In short: they MUST NOT be kept together. They start whispering in their own tongue, and within an hour any lock opens by tongue alone, and walls turn soft."}

medieval-worn-paper-name = crumpled note
medieval-worn-paper-desc = A scrap of rough grey paper thickly smeared with wet cave clay. The text is scratched in charcoal so crookedly and with such force that the paper is torn in places. The letters jump, half the words are written in uppercase mixed with lowercase, and parts of the text are rubbed away by filthy fingers.
medieval-worn-paper-content = [color=#3b3c36]mAN08 W4S KILL3D R1GH7 AW4Y. 7HEY DIDN'7 EV3N L3T H1M DRAW H1S SW0RD.

    {"TH3Y T0LD US 1N 7HE GUILD: [italic]\"1T'S JUST G0BL1NS, EV3N CH1LDR3N W1TH ST1CKS C4N DR1VE 7H3M 0FF.\"[/italic] YEAH R1GHT. 7HERE W3RE D0ZENS. 7HEY CUT D0WN 7HE WHOLE GU4RD, AND DR4GG3D US GIRLS 1NTO A H0LE. [color=#3b3c36]▒▒░░[/color]"}

    {"N0W WE 4RE 1N TH31R D3N. D4RK, ST1NKING 0F R0T AND DE4TH. TH3Y CH4INED US W1TH RUSTY 1R0N AND M4DE US H4UL ST0NE. MY H4NDS 4RE W0RN T0 BL00D."}

    {"TH3Y 4RE N0T M1NDL3SS B34STS. TH3Y 4RE SP1T3FUL, V1ND1CT1VE TH1NGS. TH3Y LAUGH WH3N TH3Y WH1P US. M4RTA FELL FR0M EXH4USTI0N AN H0UR AG0, AND TH3Y... TH3Y JUST DR4GGED H3R DE3P 1NT0 7HE C4VE. [color=#3b3c36]▓▓▒▒░[/color] ...I H34RD H3R SCR34M... ░░▒ TH3N TH3Y W3NT QU1ET."}

    {"MUST H0LD 0N. TH3Y W1LL SURELY L00K F0R US... ░░▒▓ [color=#3b3c36]...W3 C0ULDN'T JUST D1S4PPE4R L1KE TH4T...[/color][/color]"}

medieval-dirty-paper-name = filthy parchment
medieval-dirty-paper-desc = A piece of parchment soaked with damp and mold. The text is written in something rusty-brown. The handwriting has completely broken apart: huge ugly letters turn into tiny scrawls, words snap off, and chunks of text are covered in something dark and unreadable.
medieval-dirty-paper-content = [color=#5c4033]L0ST C0UNT 0F D4YS. 1T 1S ALW4YS N1GHT H3RE.

    {"Y3ST3RD4Y TH3Y THR3W US SCR4PS. I F0UND 4 PI3CE 0F M4RTA'S DR3SS 1N TH3M. I 4TE AND CR1ED, B3C4USE TH3RE 1S N0 0THER F00D. IF Y0U D0 N0T W0RK - Y0U BEC... [color=#5c4033]▓▓▓▒░░[/color] ...0ME F00D."}

    {"N0 0NE 1S C0M1NG F0R US. I UND3RST00D 1T T0D4Y WH3N I WIPED BL00D FR0M MY F4CE. H3R0ES N3ED DR4G0NS, L1CHES, D3M0NS. TH3Y N3ED GL0RY AND G0LD. N0 KN1GHT 1N SH1N1NG ARM0R W1LL C0M... [color=#5c4033]░▒▓▓▓[/color] ...E T0 A ST1NK1NG H0LE F0R A HANDFUL 0F G1RLS... T0 K1LL G0BL1NS F0R A FEW C0PPERS. W3 W1LL D1E H3RE."}

    {"TH3Y 4RE G3TT... 1NG B0LDER. 0NE 0F TH3M, HUG3, W1TH AN 1R0N CLUB... H0BG0BL1N. H3 ST4RES AT US. TH3Y 4RE HUNGRY."}

    {"G0DS, 1F Y0U 4RE TH3RE... JUST K1LL M3 1N MY SLE3P. [color=#5c4033]▓▓▒░[/color] I D0 N0T W4NT TH3M T0 E4T M3 AL1VE.[/color]"}

medieval-dirtydot-paper-name = blood-spattered sheet
medieval-dirtydot-paper-desc = A sheet of paper soaked through with fresh blood. The text is written in charcoal, but wild adrenaline and shock made the author's hand convulse. Every word is a mix of hysterical capitals, charcoal pressed deep into the paper, and spreading bloodstains.
medieval-dirtydot-paper-content = [color=#2f4f4f]SM0KE! TH3Y S3NT 1N SM0KE!

    {"I TH0UGHT TH3Y HAD DEC1DED T0 BURN US! TH3 G0BL1NS SQUE4LED, R4N AROUND, STARTED C0UGH1NG. AND TH3N [bold]H3[/bold] C4ME 0UT 0F THE SM0KE. [color=#8b0000]▓▓▒░[/color]"}

    {"1N D1RTY CH4INMAIL, 1N A DENTED H3LMET. N0 SH0UTING. N0 SPE3CHES. H3 JUST STARTED K1LL1NG TH3M. C0LDLY. L1KE A BUTCHER CH0PPING C4RCASSES."}

    {"0NE G0BL1N LE4PT 0NTO H1S BACK - H3 SM4SHED ITS H34D AGAINST TH3 TUNNEL W4LL! [color=#8b0000]▓▓▓▓▒▒░[/color] A SHAMAN STARTED MUTTERING S0METH1NG - H3 THREW A SPEAR AND P1NNED 1T T0 TH3 R0CK! WH3N H1S SW0RD WENT DULL 0N B0NE, H3 JUST THREW 1T AWAY AND T00K A DEAD G0BL1N'S WE4P0N!"}

    {"TH1S 1S N0 H3R0 FR0M T4LES! H3 1S S0ME K1ND 0F D3M0N! H3 K1LLED TH3M S0... S0 E4S1LY. TH3 H0BG0BL1N SWUNG 1TS CLUB, AND H3 CUT 1TS L3GS FR0M UNDER 1T AND DROVE A D4GGER STRA1GHT 1NT0 ITS N3CK. [color=#8b0000]▓▓▓▓▓▓▒▒▒░░[/color]"}

    {"TH3 WHOLE C4VE 1S BL00D AND GUTS. H3 ST4NDS 1N THE M1DDLE 0F 1T N0W, WIPING H1S BLADE 0N SOME RAG. H3 D1D N0T EV3N ASK H0W W3 ARE."}

    {"H3 C4ME T0 M3 AND ASKED 0NLY 0NE TH1NG:"}

    {"[italic]\"4RE TH3RE ANY M0RE G0BL1NS H3RE?\"[/italic] [color=#2f4f4f]░▒▓░[/color]"}

    {"I... W3 4RE SAVED. BUT I AM TERR1FIED T0 L00K AT H1M.[/color]"}

medieval-fatty-paper-name = greasy parchment
medieval-fatty-paper-desc = A yellowed scrap of parchment handled by filthy hands, reeking of sour ale and sewer damp. Dried mug-rings and splashes of cheap ink mark the paper. The handwriting is rough, crooked, and pressed hard.
medieval-fatty-paper-content = [color=#6b4226]Listen here, sprat. Since you found the stone in the wall and opened the hidden door, read close. This is the Gutter. Down here we are all in the same shit, and if we do not want the light dragged down on us, you will learn these rules by heart.

    {"[bold]First rule of the Gutter[/bold] - you do not tell anyone about the hidden door to the Gutter."}

    {"[bold]Second rule of the Gutter[/bold] - you do NOT, plague take you, TALK ABOUT WHAT IS UNDER THE TAVERN!"}

    {"Third rule: if someone upstairs shouts \"Guards!\", if it smells like a raid, or if a lawman comes down into the cellar, the passage closes. We bar it tight from inside. Whoever is left on the other side of the wall gets out on his own."}

    {"Fourth: go down into the cellar one at a time. A crowd draws eyes."}

    {"Fifth: no torches in the tunnels, psia krew! It stinks here for a reason - strike flint and the marsh gas gathered below will blow [color=#8b0000]▓▓▒░[/color] along with your stupid head."}

    {"Sixth rule: no coats of arms and no city colors. Below, we wear only our own cloaks. If you forgot to change your rags, they will strip them off with your skin."}

    {"Seventh: no knives in the passage. Blood draws deep rats, and we are not planning to eat those [color=#8b0000]▒▒░░[/color]."}

    {"And the eighth, most important rule. If this is your first night in the Gutter... you must bring loot.[/color]"}

medieval-necroprotocol-name = undead interrogation protocol
medieval-necroprotocol-desc = The parchment is crumpled, and in places the paper is torn by the force of the quill. The interrogator was evidently in a state of extreme fury.
medieval-necroprotocol-content = [color=#1a1a1a][color=#8b0000][head=2]Interrogation Protocol No. 84[/head][/color]

    {"[color=#5c5c5c][bold]Subject:[/bold][/color] Skeleton servant raised by necromancy."}

    {"[color=#5c5c5c][bold]Interrogator:[/bold][/color] Inquisitor Richard."}

    {"[italic]Testimony record:[/italic]"}

    {"[color=#8b0000][bold]...Twenty-eight dagger wounds![/bold][/color] You did not want to leave him even the smallest chance, did you?! Was it hatred? Rage?! He was bleeding out, begging you for mercy, but you struck again and again! I know you understand everything, you rotten scrap of bone! Confess! Confess that you killed him!"}

    {"[color=#5c5c5c]▓▒░██▒░[/color] The subject keeps a grave silence. Necrotic binding remains stable. A faint [color=#4b0082]violet flame[/color] glimmers in the empty eye sockets, and the lower jaw is missing entirely."}

    {"I demand this bastard be transferred to the executioner's torture chamber for crushing. He is clearly mocking the investigation.[/color]"}

medieval-wetpaper-name = soaked note
medieval-wetpaper-desc = A crumpled and filthy piece of cheap paper, soaked through with damp, sewer stench, and sharp vinegar. The words are written in a twitchy, tiny, very strange hand, as if scratched not with a quill, but with a sharpened bone.
medieval-wetpaper-content = [color=#5c4033][bold]Mortimir![/bold] Mortimir, listen here, you little wretch.

    {"If you found this note, then I am still down here. The Legate thought he could tax my [italic]great experiments[/italic]? The Mages' Guild thought they could lock me in a tower? To the Abyss with them!"}

    {"I have achieved [bold]absolute transmutation[/bold], Mortimir! I have skirted the laws of creation and cast off my human form to escape those dull bureaucrats!"}

    {"I scratch these lines with a rat's claw, dipping it in sewer sludge, because I no longer have proper hands. Go deeper into the sewers and look for me there. Look for something green, bumpy, and very angry! Yes, Mortimir, you understood correctly!"}

    {"I turned myself into a pickle, Mortimir! I am a pickle! I am [color=#4e8234][bolditalic]Pickle Richaard![/bolditalic][/color] [color=#2f4f4f]▓▓▓▒▒░░[/color]"}

    {"[bold]P.S.[/bold] Bring some machine oil, thread, and a couple of healing potions. I have made myself battle armor from rat bones, cartilage, and sinew to kill these things, but the knee joints squeak horribly. And hurry, the local cockroaches are starting to form an army![/color]"}

medieval-shiftedpaper-name = crumpled parchment
medieval-shiftedpaper-desc = The paper is damp, the ink bleeding into purple stains. The hand is nervous, the letters jumping - written by a wounded man cornered in a crack of stone.
medieval-shiftedpaper-content = Listen, traveler, if the Gods still hear you - do not enter the crypt beneath the church lands. I, sinful Orm of Bear Hollow, came here not for plunder, but for death, and I myself brought evil into this place.

    {"Ten of us entered under cover of night to rob the shrine guarded by the earth beneath the temple. I thought the old legends lied. But in the central chapel, beyond the altar of the ancient gods, stood burial places, and in the next hall a stone sarcophagus rose. Within lay a dead warrior, his chainmail gleaming crimson as if coals still lived inside it. On his brow rested a circlet - not gold, but pure hardened light, like the flame of sunset. Around him slept his huscarls - seven shadows in iron. Jarl Hagard Flameheart, whose name mothers whisper when laying children by the hearth... I knew him."}

    {"And among us was one I had once called friend. Sigurd, whose soul is blacker than pitch. He grinned and tore the circlet from the dead man, hissing: \"There are no more sanctities, only power.\" And then the stone drew breath."}

    {"They rose without a single cry. Only Hagard Flameheart opened his eyes - two pale sparks - and spoke in a voice that crumbled lime from the walls:"}

    {"- I and my warband, the Hird of the Holy Flame, swore to defend the gods' sanctities from corruption and to scour the Dark. Death has not lifted that oath from us. You have brought evil into this place, and evil shall be burned to ash."}

    {"Sigurd laughed, raised the stolen circlet - and fell to ash before my eyes. Flameheart does not forgive."}

    {"They hewed us down in silence, like sheaves. I managed to crawl into this hole, clutching the stump of my arm to my chest. Now the cold of the stone rises from the floor, and I hear the draugr breathing behind the wall. They wait for me to bleed out, so the sanctity can be returned to its place."}

    {"The holy guardians will not rest until the stolen thing lies where it belongs. If you are not evil - leave, and touch nothing. If there is rot in you, as there was in Sigurd... pray the Hird of the Holy Flame does not come after you into the world of the living."}

    {"... They see its light. Return it to Hagard, or they will come for everyone ..."}

medieval-lightpaper-name = bright parchment
medieval-lightpaper-desc = Covenant of Iron and Light
medieval-lightpaper-content = "Covenant of Iron and Light"

    {"I, who have accepted steel and the salt of this earth, enter beneath the shelter of the White Temple."}

    {"Nexar, whose eye is the Sun and whose voice is the silence between sword-blows, hear me."}

    {"Our creed is threefold:"}

    {"The First Covenant - Steadfastness. Our helm is iron, so neither arrow of fear nor whisper of decay may touch the mind. We are the wall between Chaos and Order."}

    {"The Second Covenant - Mercy. Our vestments are white as snow upon the world's peaks, for the hands that grip the sword also open to offer the cup. Any weary soul who enters here shall find a draught of wine to return heat to the blood, and silence to heal the spirit."}

    {"The Third Covenant - Light. The gold of the cross upon our face is no sign of pride, but a mirror. We do not judge the fallen. We light their path. Here there are no vanquished, only those who have not yet reached Rest."}

    {"I swear to be shield to the unarmed and torch to the lost. Even if the world beyond these walls turns to ash, the White Flame of Nexar burns eternal in these halls."}

    {"May thy will be as forging, and thy mercy as tempering."}

